{"resultsPerPage":7,"startIndex":0,"totalResults":7,"format":"NVD_CVE","version":"2.0","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:28:52.495","vulnerabilities":[{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-123047","sourceIdentifier":"emo@eclipse.org","published":"2026-11-05T13:17:07.493","lastModified":"2026-11-12T18:44:06.563","vulnStatus":"Deferred","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"In Eclipse BaSyx Helm Charts versions 3.0.0-rc.1 to 3.12.1 of the `basyx` chart, deployments with the bundled Keycloak enabled store the passwords of the Keycloak users that the chart creates in cleartext in a Kubernetes ConfigMap.\n\n\n\nThe template `keycloak-init-config.yaml` rendered `keycloak.initialization.users`, including each user's `credentials[].value`, as `users.json` into the persistent ConfigMap `<release>-basyx-keycloak-init-config`. By default this includes the bootstrap administrator user. That user holds the `admin` role and has a non-temporary password. A principal that can read ConfigMaps but not Secrets in the release namespace, such as a holder of the built-in Kubernetes `view` ClusterRole, can read the password from the ConfigMap and log in to Keycloak as this user. The resulting token carries the `admin` role, which the default BaSyx ABAC rules map to full rights on all BaSyx APIs in the deployment.\n\n\n\nThe bundled Keycloak is disabled by default. The issue is fixed in version 3.12.2 of the `basyx` chart, which moves the initialization users to the Keycloak credentials Secret. Affected users should upgrade and change the passwords of users that were created through the chart."}],"affected":[{"source":"emo@eclipse.org","affectedData":[{"vendor":"Eclipse Foundation","product":"Eclipse BaSyx Helm Charts","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":[{"version":"3.0.0-rc.1","lessThan":"3.12.2","versionType":"custom","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"emo@eclipse.org","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","baseScore":7.5,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"HIGH","privilegesRequired":"LOW","userInteraction":"NONE","scope":"UNCHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"HIGH","integrityImpact":"HIGH","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":1.6,"impactScore":5.9}],"ssvcV203":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","ssvcData":{"timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:54:46.133265Z","id":"CVE-2026-123047","options":[{"exploitation":"none"},{"automatable":"no"},{"technicalImpact":"total"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","version":"2.0.3"}}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"emo@eclipse.org","type":"Secondary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-312"},{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-522"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/eclipse-basyx/charts/pull/106","source":"emo@eclipse.org"},{"url":"https://github.com/eclipse-basyx/charts/releases/tag/basyx-3.12.2","source":"emo@eclipse.org"},{"url":"https://github.com/eclipse-basyx/charts/security/advisories/GHSA-6438-759f-6f8v","source":"emo@eclipse.org"},{"url":"https://gitlab.eclipse.org/security/cve-assignment/-/work_items/547","source":"emo@eclipse.org"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-123059","sourceIdentifier":"emo@eclipse.org","published":"2026-11-05T14:17:04.940","lastModified":"2026-11-12T18:44:06.563","vulnStatus":"Deferred","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"In Eclipse BaSyx Helm Charts version 2.2.0 of the `aas-basyx-v2-full` chart, deployments with the bundled Keycloak enabled store the client secret of the `basyx-technical-user` OAuth2 client in cleartext in a Kubernetes ConfigMap. This client uses the client-credentials grant and its service account holds the realm `admin` role.\n\n\n\nThe chart correctly writes `keycloak.technicalUser.clientSecret` to a Kubernetes Secret, but the template `basyx-keycloak-realm.yaml` also substitutes the same value into the Keycloak realm-import JSON, which is stored in the ConfigMap `<keycloak.fullnameOverride>-realm`. A principal that can read ConfigMaps but not Secrets in the release namespace, such as a holder of the built-in Kubernetes `view` ClusterRole, can read the client secret from the ConfigMap. They can then exchange it at the Keycloak token endpoint for an access token with the `admin` role. That token grants full create, read, update, delete and execute rights on all BaSyx repositories and registries in the deployment.\n\n\n\nThe bundled Keycloak is disabled by default. No fixed release of the `aas-basyx-v2-full` chart exists. Affected users should migrate to the `basyx` chart, or deploy without the bundled Keycloak and rotate the `basyx-technical-user` client secret."}],"affected":[{"source":"emo@eclipse.org","affectedData":[{"vendor":"Eclipse Foundation","product":"Eclipse BaSyx Helm Charts","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":[{"version":"2.2.0","versionType":"semver","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"emo@eclipse.org","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","baseScore":7.5,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"HIGH","privilegesRequired":"LOW","userInteraction":"NONE","scope":"UNCHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"HIGH","integrityImpact":"HIGH","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":1.6,"impactScore":5.9}],"ssvcV203":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","ssvcData":{"timestamp":"2026-11-05T21:24:06.286598Z","id":"CVE-2026-123059","options":[{"exploitation":"none"},{"automatable":"no"},{"technicalImpact":"total"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","version":"2.0.3"}}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"emo@eclipse.org","type":"Secondary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-312"},{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-522"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/eclipse-basyx/charts/pull/46","source":"emo@eclipse.org"},{"url":"https://github.com/eclipse-basyx/charts/releases/tag/aas-basyx-v2-full-2.2.0","source":"emo@eclipse.org"},{"url":"https://github.com/eclipse-basyx/charts/security/advisories/GHSA-6438-759f-6f8v","source":"emo@eclipse.org"},{"url":"https://gitlab.eclipse.org/security/cve-assignment/-/work_items/546","source":"emo@eclipse.org"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-58490","sourceIdentifier":"security-advisories@github.com","published":"2026-11-06T20:17:23.253","lastModified":"2026-11-12T22:18:51.470","vulnStatus":"Deferred","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Tracecat is an open-source security automation platform for teams and AI agents. From version 0.37.0 until 1.0.0-beta.49, Docker Compose deployments with SAML enabled can render SAML_SIGNED_ASSERTIONS and SAML_SIGNED_RESPONSES as empty values, overriding secure application defaults and disabling both signature requirements. An unauthenticated attacker who can reach the SAML assertion consumer endpoint can submit a forged unsigned response for an existing Tracecat user email address and obtain that user’s session. Targeting an existing superadmin can result in superadmin account takeover. Exploitation does not create users when SAML user creation is disabled and does not affect default Fargate or Helm deployments. Version 1.0.0-beta.49 removes the insecure deployment pass-through and requires signed assertions and responses."}],"affected":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"TracecatHQ","product":"tracecat","versions":[{"version":">= 0.37.0, < 1.0.0-beta.49","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","baseScore":9.8,"baseSeverity":"CRITICAL","attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"NONE","userInteraction":"NONE","scope":"UNCHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"HIGH","integrityImpact":"HIGH","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":5.9}],"ssvcV203":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","ssvcData":{"timestamp":"2026-11-09T13:19:25.003724Z","id":"CVE-2026-58490","options":[{"exploitation":"none"},{"automatable":"yes"},{"technicalImpact":"total"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","version":"2.0.3"}}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-347"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/TracecatHQ/tracecat/commit/018258ba6a17c36cbfa7ca977526c34fb6afc35f","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/TracecatHQ/tracecat/commit/a97aafbfd667a6b9a3b7b524e1c1bfa9d8c59779","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/TracecatHQ/tracecat/commit/dab64eb7ac0eb2088783ca14f4cb2d058547bfff","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/TracecatHQ/tracecat/pull/2824","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/TracecatHQ/tracecat/pull/2825","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/TracecatHQ/tracecat/pull/2826","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/TracecatHQ/tracecat/releases/tag/1.0.0-beta.49","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/TracecatHQ/tracecat/security/advisories/GHSA-6g53-h6fh-c3pj","source":"security-advisories@github.com"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-65960","sourceIdentifier":"security-advisories@github.com","published":"2026-11-06T20:17:24.397","lastModified":"2026-11-12T22:18:35.610","vulnStatus":"Awaiting Analysis","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Tetragon is an eBPF-based security observability and runtime enforcement project. Versions before 1.7.0 can use a Helm default that exposes the privileged Tetragon gRPC API through an unauthenticated TCP listener on localhost:54321. An attacker who can run or compromise same-node hostNetwork pods can reach the listener and invoke privileged methods without authentication. These methods can add, delete, or reconfigure tracing policies and change debug settings, potentially resulting in privilege escalation or container escape. Version 1.7.0 changes the default endpoint to a Unix-domain socket. Deployments that do not expose an unauthenticated TCP listener are not affected."}],"affected":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"cilium","product":"tetragon","versions":[{"version":"< 1.7.0","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H","baseScore":8.8,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","attackVector":"LOCAL","attackComplexity":"LOW","privilegesRequired":"LOW","userInteraction":"NONE","scope":"CHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"HIGH","integrityImpact":"HIGH","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":2.0,"impactScore":6.0}],"ssvcV203":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","ssvcData":{"timestamp":"2026-11-10T20:07:08.800655Z","id":"CVE-2026-65960","options":[{"exploitation":"none"},{"automatable":"no"},{"technicalImpact":"total"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","version":"2.0.3"}}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-306"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/cilium/tetragon/commit/8e89933d3526f37c04f7523013ff32f8b1c6f62a","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/cilium/tetragon/commit/fe46101770b960ebbf39fe9749bb20d49cf178b2","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/cilium/tetragon/pull/4882","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/cilium/tetragon/releases/tag/v1.7.0","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/cilium/tetragon/security/advisories/GHSA-6qqg-3qf7-p3v5","source":"security-advisories@github.com"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-129236","sourceIdentifier":"security-advisories@github.com","published":"2026-11-16T17:17:31.313","lastModified":"2026-11-17T17:18:02.187","vulnStatus":"Received","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Kubeshark is an eBPF-powered network observability tool for Kubernetes. From 53.1.0 until 53.4.0, the start_kubeshark MCP tool in cmd/mcpRunner.go uses callStartKubeshark to append caller-controlled pod_regex as a bare positional argument to kubeshark tap without a -- end-of-options separator, allowing a value beginning with --set to be parsed as a Helm value override. An attacker who influences tool arguments against kubeshark mcp --allow-destructive can redirect the privileged worker, Hub, and front images through tap.docker.registry and tap.docker.tag to an attacker-controlled registry. Because the deployed worker DaemonSet runs privileged with host networking and host filesystem access, a malicious image can obtain node and cluster-admin access when the host already has permission to deploy it. This issue is fixed in version 53.4.0."}],"affected":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"kubeshark","product":"kubeshark","versions":[{"version":">= 53.1.0, < 53.4.0","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV31":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"3.1","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:H/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H","baseScore":7.2,"baseSeverity":"HIGH","attackVector":"LOCAL","attackComplexity":"HIGH","privilegesRequired":"HIGH","userInteraction":"REQUIRED","scope":"CHANGED","confidentialityImpact":"HIGH","integrityImpact":"HIGH","availabilityImpact":"HIGH"},"exploitabilityScore":0.6,"impactScore":6.0}],"ssvcV203":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","ssvcData":{"timestamp":"2026-11-17T16:06:27.490825Z","id":"CVE-2026-129236","options":[{"exploitation":"none"},{"automatable":"no"},{"technicalImpact":"total"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","version":"2.0.3"}}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-88"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/kubeshark/kubeshark/commit/a76a1920dc7587be700a17f1592f58a9512ad214","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/kubeshark/kubeshark/pull/1957","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/kubeshark/kubeshark/releases/tag/v53.4.0","source":"security-advisories@github.com"},{"url":"https://github.com/kubeshark/kubeshark/security/advisories/GHSA-8vf2-hxg5-crqh","source":"security-advisories@github.com"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-120753","sourceIdentifier":"emo@eclipse.org","published":"2026-11-19T15:17:25.013","lastModified":"2026-11-19T20:17:21.490","vulnStatus":"Received","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"In Eclipse Ditto versions 1.1.0 to 3.9.8, when pre-authentication is enabled, the gateway service accepts the pre-authenticated subject not only from the `x-ditto-pre-authenticated` HTTP header set by a trusted reverse proxy, but also from an undocumented `x-ditto-pre-authenticated` URL query parameter that a client can set. A reverse proxy that only overwrites the header therefore does not stop clients from supplying their own subject. With the default configuration of the Ditto Helm chart (`global.jwtOnly: false`, which implicitly enables pre-authentication), the bundled nginx skips HTTP Basic authentication for any request with an `Authorization: Bearer` header and forwards it without the pre-authentication header. An unauthenticated remote attacker can send an invalid Bearer token together with the query parameter to authenticate as any chosen policy subject. Pre-authentication succeeds before the JWT is validated, so the attacker can read and modify Things and Policies with that subject's permissions. As a mitigation, disable pre-authentication in the gateway (`ENABLE_PRE_AUTHENTICATION=false`) or, when using the Helm chart, configure `global.jwtOnly: true`."}],"affected":[{"source":"emo@eclipse.org","affectedData":[{"vendor":"Eclipse Foundation","product":"Eclipse Ditto","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":[{"version":"1.1.0","lessThanOrEqual":"3.9.8","versionType":"semver","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV40":[{"source":"emo@eclipse.org","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"4.0","vectorString":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","baseScore":9.1,"baseSeverity":"CRITICAL","attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"LOW","attackRequirements":"PRESENT","privilegesRequired":"NONE","userInteraction":"NONE","vulnConfidentialityImpact":"HIGH","vulnIntegrityImpact":"HIGH","vulnAvailabilityImpact":"NONE","subConfidentialityImpact":"NONE","subIntegrityImpact":"NONE","subAvailabilityImpact":"NONE","exploitMaturity":"NOT_DEFINED","confidentialityRequirement":"NOT_DEFINED","integrityRequirement":"NOT_DEFINED","availabilityRequirement":"NOT_DEFINED","modifiedAttackVector":"NOT_DEFINED","modifiedAttackComplexity":"NOT_DEFINED","modifiedAttackRequirements":"NOT_DEFINED","modifiedPrivilegesRequired":"NOT_DEFINED","modifiedUserInteraction":"NOT_DEFINED","modifiedVulnConfidentialityImpact":"NOT_DEFINED","modifiedVulnIntegrityImpact":"NOT_DEFINED","modifiedVulnAvailabilityImpact":"NOT_DEFINED","modifiedSubConfidentialityImpact":"NOT_DEFINED","modifiedSubIntegrityImpact":"NOT_DEFINED","modifiedSubAvailabilityImpact":"NOT_DEFINED","Safety":"NOT_DEFINED","Automatable":"NOT_DEFINED","Recovery":"NOT_DEFINED","valueDensity":"NOT_DEFINED","vulnerabilityResponseEffort":"NOT_DEFINED","providerUrgency":"NOT_DEFINED"}}],"ssvcV203":[{"source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0","ssvcData":{"timestamp":"2026-11-19T20:09:50.909629Z","id":"CVE-2026-120753","options":[{"exploitation":"poc"},{"automatable":"no"},{"technicalImpact":"total"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","version":"2.0.3"}}]},"weaknesses":[{"source":"emo@eclipse.org","type":"Secondary","description":[{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-287"},{"lang":"en","value":"CWE-290"}]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/eclipse-ditto/ditto/security/advisories/GHSA-chwq-wg27-qvfr","source":"emo@eclipse.org"},{"url":"https://gitlab.eclipse.org/security/cve-assignment/-/work_items/539","source":"emo@eclipse.org"},{"url":"https://gitlab.eclipse.org/security/vulnerability-reports/-/work_items/1346","source":"emo@eclipse.org"},{"url":"https://gitlab.eclipse.org/security/vulnerability-reports/-/work_items/1346","source":"134c704f-9b21-4f2e-91b3-4a467353bcc0"}]}},{"cve":{"id":"CVE-2026-134756","sourceIdentifier":"disclosure@vulncheck.com","published":"2026-11-22T15:17:13.953","lastModified":"2026-11-24T01:17:29.220","vulnStatus":"Received","cveTags":[],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"Portainer Community Edition and Business Edition 2.39.0 before 2.45.1 contain a server-side request forgery vulnerability because user-supplied URLs are only syntax-checked by validate.IsURL without resolved address validation. Authenticated users can abuse Git cloning, Helm retrieval, registry ping, or the GitLab proxy to reach loopback, internal, and cloud metadata addresses, probing ports and reading responses."}],"affected":[{"source":"disclosure@vulncheck.com","affectedData":[{"vendor":"portainer","product":"portainer","defaultStatus":"unaffected","repo":"https://github.com/portainer/portainer","packageURL":"pkg:golang/github.com/portainer/portainer","versions":[{"version":"2.39.0","lessThan":"2.45.1","versionType":"semver","status":"affected"}]}]}],"metrics":{"cvssMetricV40":[{"source":"disclosure@vulncheck.com","type":"Secondary","cvssData":{"version":"4.0","vectorString":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","baseScore":5.3,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","attackVector":"NETWORK","attackComplexity":"LOW","attackRequirements":"NO